**Amendment (Comparison evidence)** · `amend:devperf:comparison-evidence` The reporter appends comparison assessments to .lane/performance-assessments.jsonl separately from raw results and .lane/performance-findings.jsonl. Missing measurements or baselines, noisy clocks, incompatible cache states and unestablished comparisons are explicitly inconclusive; budget excess still warns and a completed functional result remains completed. Comparable regression evidence requires an explicitly compatible baseline with at least five samples; no gate run manufactures one. Baseline fields and original observations are retained, not replaced automatically. The support step provides benchmark workloads and smoke under (`rule:harness:benchmarks`); reviewed comparable baselines remain absent and their comparison is inconclusive rather than invented evidence. Doctest accounting uses the committed prior roster and refuses missing required execution just like nextest. Identity is the lexically normalized file path, item (or module for file documentation) and one-based example ordinal in source-line order within that item. Line numbers select the ordinal but are not identity; unrelated line shifts preserve names. Duplicate source positions and normalized identities are structural errors, and adding or removing an example still requires a reviewed roster change. Raw rustdoc names remain in retained evidence. The runner checks cargo-nextest exactly 0.9.149 before building or executing against its experimental stream; a different version is a named structural refusal. The owned warning path is implemented for current declared suites; property and benchmark support is now implemented, while the remaining holds are stated in (`amend:harness:matrix-evidence`).


